.TH READLINKAT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
readlinkat \- read a directory-relative symbolic link
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.BI "ssize_t readlinkat(int " directory ", const char* " path ","
.BI "                char* " buffer ", size_t " byte_count ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Resolves a relative link path from an open directory descriptor, or from the
current directory if it is
.BR AT_FDCWD .
An absolute path ignores the descriptor.
The caller supplies enough writable storage for the count.
At most that many bytes are copied; no NUL terminator is appended. A result
equal to the buffer size may indicate truncation.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the byte count on success, leaving
.B errno
unchanged, or \-1 on failure with positive Linux
.BR errno .
.SH NOTES
Crunch errno is process\-wide.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR readlink (3crunch),
.BR symlinkat (3crunch),
.BR readlinkat (2)
